{#
    One <td> per chosen column per warehouse, driven by `columns` — the resolved registry from
    InventoryGridColumns, which the header row, the filter row's colspan and the empty state below
    are all driven by as well (#36).

    It used to be nine hand-written cells. That is why seven of the fourteen quantities on
    product_inventory never appeared: adding a bucket to the entity changed nothing here, and
    nothing anywhere said so. Now a bucket with no column fails
    InventoryGridBucketCoverageCest by name, and a column with no cell fails it too.

    `data-column` is on every warehouse cell and `data-avail-sign` on every BUCKET one, so the
    reconciliation can be read off the rendered page rather than recomputed from the entity: the
    test adds sign × value across the row and asserts the total is the Available cell. Two
    independent computations of one number is the only kind of check that can catch either one
    being wrong. The sign is the EFFECTIVE one for this row — 0 where a bundle is Inactive and the
    term has left getAvailableQuantity() — which is what makes the same assertion hold under the
    bundles-off run.
#}
{% for row in rows %}
    <tr class="data-item-row">
        <td data-label="ID" class="searchable">{{ row.id }}</td>
        <td data-label="Product name" class="product-name-cell searchable">{{ row.name }}</td>
        <td data-label="SKU" class="searchable">{{ row.sku }}</td>
        <td data-label="Category" class="searchable">{{ row.category|default('-') }}</td>
        {% for warehouse in warehouses %}
            {% set bucket = row.qtyByWarehouse[warehouse.id] %}
            {% set startingQuantity = bucket.cells.starting.value|qty %}
            {% for col in columns %}
                {% set cell = bucket.cells[col.key] %}
                {% set label = warehouse.name ~ ' — ' ~ col.label %}
                {#- The "not counted" class is per ROW, not per column: the three bundle-gated terms
                    leave getAvailableQuantity() the moment their bundle goes Inactive, and nothing
                    is zeroed when they do. A column reading 40 that availability is ignoring is the
                    reconciliation defect in miniature, so the cell says so rather than looking like
                    a term that simply did not add up. -#}
                {% set stateClass = col.kind == 'bucket' and cell.sign == 0 ? ' is-not-counted' : '' %}

                {% if col.key == 'starting' %}
                    {# For a dimensional product (#550) the number is maintained by the depth layer, not
                       typed — so the editable box is replaced by a link to the breakdown that maintains it.
                       bucket.breakdownUrl is null for every product on simple inventory, which is every
                       product until someone opts one in, and is null again the moment the depth bundle is
                       removed. #}
                    {% if bucket.breakdownUrl|default(null) is not empty %}
                        <td data-label="{{ label }}" data-column="starting" data-avail-sign="{{ cell.sign }}" class="inventory-dimensional-cell">
                            <a class="price-display" href="{{ bucket.breakdownUrl }}" title="Maintained by bin, lot and serial — open the breakdown to adjust it">{{ startingQuantity }}</a>
                            {# Hidden, not absent, and carrying the id the quantity box would have had.
                               postBackorderSetting() reads that id to echo the current quantity back with a
                               settings change; with no element it falls back to data-current-quantity on the
                               control itself, which is what makes the backorder columns safe to show while
                               Starting is hidden. The backorder settings are orthogonal to HOW the quantity
                               is maintained, so they stay editable here — this is what lets them be, safely. #}
                            <input type="hidden" id="inv_{{ row.id }}_{{ warehouse.id }}" value="{{ startingQuantity }}">
                        </td>
                    {% else %}
                        <td data-label="{{ label }}" data-column="starting" data-avail-sign="{{ cell.sign }}">
                            <button type="button" class="price-display js-inventory-display" data-target-input="inv_{{ row.id }}_{{ warehouse.id }}">{{ startingQuantity }}</button>
                            <input
                                id="inv_{{ row.id }}_{{ warehouse.id }}"
                                class="price-input js-inventory-input"
                                type="number"
                                min="0"
                                step="1"
                                value="{{ startingQuantity }}"
                                data-product-id="{{ row.id }}"
                                data-warehouse-id="{{ warehouse.id }}">
                        </td>
                    {% endif %}
                {% elseif col.kind == 'derived' %}
                    {# Available. Not a stored figure and not recomputed in the template either — it is
                       ProductInventory::getAvailableQuantity(), carried through. The title spells the
                       row's own arithmetic out so the number can be checked without counting columns.

                       The `off page` note is the chooser's one dangerous edge made visible: hide
                       Quarantine on a row holding 12 quarantined units and Available is 12 short of
                       everything on screen, which is precisely the defect this issue exists to end —
                       reintroduced by the feature that makes the rest of it bearable. So the gap is
                       stated, with the buckets that carry it named, rather than left to be found. #}
                    <td data-label="{{ label }}" data-column="{{ col.key }}"
                        class="inventory-readonly-cell inventory-available-cell{{ bucket.available < 0 ? ' is-oversold' : '' }}{{ bucket.offPage.amount != 0 ? ' has-off-page-terms' : '' }}"
                        data-off-page="{{ bucket.offPage.amount }}"
                        title="{{ bucket.working }}"><strong>{{ bucket.available|qty }}</strong>{% if bucket.offPage.amount != 0 %}<span class="inventory-off-page-note">{{ bucket.offPage.amount > 0 ? '+' : '−' }}{{ bucket.offPage.amount|abs }} off page: {{ bucket.offPage.labels|join(', ') }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
                {% elseif col.kind == 'setting' %}
                    {# One control, one column. All four used to be stacked in a single cell, which meant
                       none of them could be hidden on its own and the four read as one setting with
                       decoration. data-current-quantity is what lets a control be shown while the Starting
                       column is not: the endpoint validates a quantity on every save, and reading it off a
                       box that is no longer on the page would post 0 and zero the stock. #}
                    <td data-label="{{ label }}" data-column="{{ col.key }}" class="inventory-backorder-cell">
                        {% if col.key == 'max_backorder' %}
                            <input type="number" class="js-backorder-setting" data-field="max_backorder_quantity"
                                min="0" step="1" placeholder="No cap" value="{{ cell.value is null ? '' : cell.value|qty }}"
                                aria-label="{{ label }}"
                                data-product-id="{{ row.id }}" data-warehouse-id="{{ warehouse.id }}"
                                data-current-quantity="{{ startingQuantity }}">
                        {% else %}
                            {% set field = col.key == 'allow_backorder' ? 'allow_backorder' : (col.key == 'backorder_cap_shrinks' ? 'backorder_cap_shrinks_on_restock' : 'auto_release_on_restock') %}
                            <input type="checkbox" class="js-backorder-setting" data-field="{{ field }}"
                                aria-label="{{ label }}"
                                data-product-id="{{ row.id }}" data-warehouse-id="{{ warehouse.id }}"
                                data-current-quantity="{{ startingQuantity }}"{{ cell.value ? ' checked' : '' }}>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                {% else %}
                    {# Every other bucket. Readonly: what is held, promised, quarantined or written off is
                       decided by the documents and the movements, never typed here. #}
                    <td data-label="{{ label }}" data-column="{{ col.key }}" data-avail-sign="{{ cell.sign }}"
                        class="inventory-readonly-cell{{ stateClass }}"
                        {%- if col.kind == 'bucket' and cell.sign == 0 %} title="Not counted in Available. {{ col.note }}"{% endif %}>{{ cell.value|qty }}</td>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
    </tr>
{% else %}
    <tr>
        <td colspan="{{ 4 + warehouses|length * columns|length }}" class="empty-table-cell">
            <strong>No products found.</strong>
            <span>Products will appear here once created.</span>
        </td>
    </tr>
{% endfor %}
